.TH SDL_FilterEvents 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_FilterEvents \- Run a specific filter function on the current event queue, removing any events for which the filter returns false.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_FilterEvents(SDL_EventFilter filter, void *userdata);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
See
.BR SDL_SetEventFilter ()
for more information\[char46] Unlike
.BR SDL_SetEventFilter (),
this function does not change the filter permanently, it only uses the supplied filter until this function returns\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I filter
the
.BR SDL_EventFilter
function to call when an event happens\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
a pointer that is passed to
.BR filter \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetEventFilter (3),
.BR SDL_SetEventFilter (3)
